*** URAM CRITICAL FAILURE ***
The design requested 776 URAMs but Versal xcvc1902 only has 463. This is
PHYSICALLY UN-IMPLEMENTABLE — vivado place-and-route would fail.

Root cause: my `ffn_h[256][1536]` array (384 KB total) had:
    #pragma HLS BIND_STORAGE variable=ffn_h type=RAM_T2P impl=URAM
    #pragma HLS ARRAY_PARTITION variable=ffn_h cyclic factor=64 dim=2
Together these create 64 separate URAM banks, each at MINIMUM 1 URAM (32 KB)
even though each bank only holds ~6 KB of data. 64 banks × ~12 URAMs per bank
for true-2-port = 768 URAMs. Plus 8 more for some metadata.

The intent was "store ffn_h in URAM to avoid BRAM pressure", but partitioning
into 64 banks made it WORSE than BRAM.

